// "mills" — the third-person mill verb phrase ([CR#701.17a]: that player
// puts that many cards from the top of their library into their
// graveyard). A parse/render TEMPLATE over the core `Mill` player action:
// the declarative-subject production parses "target player / each
// opponent / each player" into the agent, matches the remaining verb
// phrase against this template, and emits `By(<agent>, Mills(n))`, which
// expands in place to `By(<agent>, Mill(n))` — kind `PlayerAction` has no
// remembered-expansion wrapper, so the macro is pure spelling sugar.
(
    name: "Mills",
    template: "mills ${0:card|cards}",
    kinds: [PlayerAction],
    params: [Count],
    body: Mill(Param(0)),
)
